<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Copper plate inscriptions</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> plate inscriptions are legal records engraved on copper sheets, used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> to document royal land grants. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> they recorded grants of land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> priests and Buddhist monasteries. Such grants functioned as a mechanism of tax administration, delegating revenue collection and local governance to religious institutions.</p></div>
